dcrumb_text text-size-small text-weight-medium text-color-shade-40">/</p><p class="breadcrumb_text text-size-small text-weight-medium">AI Copyright Risks in Ecommerce: The Rights Matrix</p></div><div class="blog-post_wrap"><div class="blog-post_content-wrap"><div data-wf--card-blog--variant="blog-post-header" class="slider_item"><div class="blog-card w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><div class="blog-card_img-wrap w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><img loading="eager" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/69cfafd4ed3be7bbd72d539f/6ad85c3a1cef3c69ff6f3409_row-167-AI%20Copyright%20Risks%2C%20Mapped.png" alt="" class="blog-card_img w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"/></div><div class="blog-card_content-wrap w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><div class="blog-card_info-wrap w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><text class="blog-card_info-text text-size-small text-color-shade-70 w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><span>October 21, 2026</span><span> • </span><span>9</span><span> min read</span></text><div class="blog-card_btn-wrap w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><a href="/authors/nawras-ganim" class="blog-card_author-link w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7 w-inline-block"><By class="blog-card_author-text text-size-small text-color-shade-70 w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><span>By</span></By><div data-wf--icon-main--variant="1-25rem" class="icon-wrap w-variant-a56152a4-aef1-e6bf-1b29-1a064f3d1908 radius-round"><img loading="lazy" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/69cfafd4ed3be7bbd72d539f/69d5fcff2b7daf8856faa007_Nawras%20Ganim.webp" alt="" class="icon-image w-variant-a56152a4-aef1-e6bf-1b29-1a064f3d1908"/></div><By class="blog-card_author-text text-size-small text-color-shade-70 w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7"><span>Nawras Ganim</span></By></a></div></div><h1 class="blog-card_heading w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7">AI Copyright Risks in Ecommerce: The Rights Matrix</h1><p class="blog-card_paragraph w-variant-53a43be5-6944-1410-e4e8-568d9ed40ea7  ">Use a five-part rights matrix to assess an AI asset’s source, model terms, copyright status, third-party rights, and publishing rules.</p></div></div></div><div toc="content" class="text-rich-text w-richtext"><p>AI copyright risks in ecommerce sit at five points in an asset&#x27;s path from source to storefront. You need to check the input, the model terms, the output&#x27;s copyright status, any likeness or trademark, and the publishing channel.</p><p>I&#x27;ve run two Shopify stores and required a supplier email or license before treating a product photo as cleared for use. Use the five checks below to decide whether you can publish one image, description, or ad clip. The label &quot;AI-generated&quot; doesn&#x27;t settle that decision by itself.</p><h2>Key takeaways</h2><div class="w-embed"><style>
